  "name": "Anthro Northwest",
  "shortName": "ANW",
  "description": "Anthro Northwest (ANW) is an annual family-friendly anthropomorphic art convention in Seattle, Washington, rated PG at most. It was founded to promote charity, hospitality and creativity through art, education and community building, and is run by Anthro Northwest Charities, a 501(c)(3) organization. Since its start it has partnered with Sarvey Wildlife, a wildlife rehabilitation center, and had raised $75,738 for it as of 2025. Distinctive features include a Thanksgiving feast, the Anthro National Film Festival, Andy's Adventureland, fine arts panels, a 24/7 art jam room, a children's track and a fursuit exhibition. The first convention was held November 9 to 12, 2017, at the Seattle Renaissance Hotel, and recent editions have taken place at the Hyatt Regency Seattle.",
